X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/events/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260410T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260529T163000
DTSTAMP:20260406T231345
CREATED:20260211T162632Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260216T211221Z
UID:142084-1775827800-1780072200@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:Hand Building (Beginner)
DESCRIPTION:Hand Building (Beginner)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Fridays April 10 to May 29\, 2026\n1:30 pm – 4:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nFor ages 18+ \nLearn to make functional\, sculptural\, and decorative pieces using hand-building techniques. Practice sculpting\, slab building\, coiling\, surface decoration\, and glazing. This 8-week class is designed for students new to ceramics. \n\nThis class includes access to a 10kg bag of clay\, glazes and underglazes. Additional bags can be purchased for $35 each. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $412\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $485\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    SOLD OUT\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: April 10\, 17\, 24\, May 1\, 8\, 15\, 22\, 29 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class Outline: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nWeek 1: Slab building\nWeek 2: Coil building\nWeek 3: Surface decoration\nWeek 4: Pinch pot forms\nWeek 5: Using clay templates\nWeek 6: Applying underglaze\nWeek 7: Exploring functional and nonfunctional works\nWeek 8: Glazing\n\n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $50 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase adult clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Natalie Fisher\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Natalie is a passionate young artist with more than 15 years of experience teaching art to students of all ages. She is formally trained in drawing\, painting\, photography\, printmaking\, and sculpture. She recently received her Masters in Expressive Arts Therapy from the University of Hong Kong. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/hand-building-beginner-spring-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Adult Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Adult-Class-Thumbnail-15.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
