CREATED:20260113T173358Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260113T173358Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a5f4f98089f23c675f5344"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Innovator in Residence Kick-Off Party!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260411T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260411T140000
UID:69a5f4f98089f23c675f5344@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What happens when a professional composer with over 25 years i
 n film and television music meets artificial intelligence? It's complicate
 d.\nJoin Joel S. Silver\, TPL's Spring 2026 Innovator in Residence\, for t
 he launch of a 12-week residency exploring AI and music production at Fair
 view's Digital Innovation Hub. Joel has composed music for productions acr
 oss CBC\, Netflix\, and NBC\, and has spent the last decade navigating AI'
 s growing role in the creative process — sometimes embracing it\, someti
 mes wrestling with it\, and always asking hard questions about what it mea
 ns for musicians and creators.\nIn this opening event\, Joel will share hi
 s journey from traditional composing to working with AI tools\, including 
 live examples of how he's used AI in his own professional music. Then it's
  your turn - you'll get a chance to try AI music tools for yourself and he
 ar what they can do. Whether you're a musician\, a curious beginner\, or s
 omeone with strong opinions about AI\, this is your invitation to join the
  conversation.\nThis program is part of the Innovator in Residence (AI and
  Music Production) program\, which is designed to help beginner and interm
 ediate learners build knowledge and creative skills and get hands-on with 
 current AI tools in music production and learn about the history\, copyrig
 ht and ethics of generative music. For more information and a full list of
  programs\, visit\ntpl.ca/airesident\n.
LOCATION:Fairview\, 1st Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a5f4f98089f23c675f5344
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Batashoemuseum": "https://batashoemuseum.ca/event/perfume-creation-with-orris-labs/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:batashoemuseum
X-SOURCE:Bata Shoe Museum
X-SOURCE-URL:https://batashoemuseum.ca/events/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260411T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260411T153000
DTSTAMP:20260406T231352
CREATED:20251114T204019Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251218T203654Z
UID:15850-1775912400-1775921400@batashoemuseum.ca
SUMMARY:Perfume Creation with Orris Labs
DESCRIPTION:Date: Saturday\, April 11\, 2026\nTime: 1:00 pm – 3:30 pm\nLocation: Bata Shoe Museum\, 327 Bloor St. W.\nTickets: $70 \nIn celebration of André Perugia: A Design Legend Unveiled—and inspired by Perugia’s own ventures into perfumery—Orris Labs invites you to create your own signature fragrance in this immersive\, hands-on workshop. \nGuided by expert perfumers\, you’ll explore many fragrance notes and learn the art of scent blending\, from balancing top\, heart\, and base notes to layering aromas that reflect your individual style. As you craft your one-of-a-kind perfume\, discover how elegance\, innovation\, and artistry connect the worlds of footwear and fragrance. \nMuseum admission\, materials\, instruction\, and light refreshments are all included. Limited spots available — reserve your place for this exclusive multisensory experience today. This workshop is recommended for 18+. \nBUY YOUR TICKETS  \n\nABOUT ORRIS LABS: \nOrris Labs is a Canadian-owned perfume and cologne workshop that offers a hands-on experience in the art of fragrance creation. Participants are guided through the fascinating world of perfumery\, learning about scent notes\, blending techniques\, and the history of fragrance. With access to over 50 different oils and aromatic compounds\, guests have the opportunity to experiment and craft a personalized scent that reflects their individual style and personality\, all under the guidance of an experienced perfumer. \nProudly Canadian\, Orris Labs partners with local suppliers and small businesses to support growth\, sustainability\, and community vibrancy within the Canadian economy. By taking part in an Orris Labs workshop\, guests not only leave with their own custom fragrance and a deeper appreciation for the art of perfumery but also contribute to the success of local enterprises across the country. \n\nPlease review our Terms and Conditions in advance and check in with Visitor Services upon arrival. Questions? Email us info@batashoemuseum.ca anytime.
URL:https://batashoemuseum.ca/event/perfume-creation-with-orris-labs/
CATEGORIES:Workshops
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://batashoemuseum.ca/wp-content/uploads/BSM_Perfume_banner-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
