SUMMARY:Teen Wheel Throwing (13 - 17)
DESCRIPTION:Teen Wheel Throwing (13 – 17)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Saturdays April 11 to June 6\, 2026\n1:30 pm – 4:00 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    For ages 13 – 17 \nExpress your creativity on the pottery wheel in this 8-week class! Learn wheel-throwing techniques to create your own functional\, sculptural\, and decorative pottery. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $360\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $306\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    SOLD OUT\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: April 11\, 18\, 25\, May 2\, 9\, 23\, 30\, June 6\nNo class on May 16 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $30 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nUsing the pottery wheel may cause serious injury to a person who has a pacemaker. Consult a physician before use.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase kids clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders’ children and grandchildren. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Natalie Fisher\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Natalie is a passionate young artist with more than 15 years of experience teaching art to students of all ages. She is formally trained in drawing\, painting\, photography\, printmaking\, and sculpture. She recently received her Masters in Expressive Arts Therapy from the University of Hong Kong. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/teen-wheel-throwing-13-17-spring-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Kids Classes
