DESCRIPTION:After learning the fundamentals about video editing in part on
 e\, we’ll continue to explore adding elements to the timeline such as gr
 aphics.\nAfter learning the fundamentals about video editing in part one\,
  we’ll continue to explore adding elements to the timeline such as graph
 ics.  Learn how to customize effects and transitions by adding keyframes.\
 nHow to use the Ultra Key/Chroma Key to remove a background color such as 
 a video using a Green Screen.  Fix shaky footage with the Warp Stabilizer 
 and have your video looking sharper and more professional than ever.\nLast
 ly we’ll explore how to edit a video with multiple video channels by uti
 lizing the Multi-Camera editing feature in Adobe Premiere\nAges 13+\nRegis
 tration is required for this class.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe p
 ersonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Librar
