X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardinermuseum": "https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/the-gardiner-transformed-curator-tour-and-hands-on-clay-session-april-14-2026/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardinermuseum
X-SOURCE:Gardiner Museum
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/events/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260414T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260414T193000
DTSTAMP:20260406T231346
CREATED:20260126T202735Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260126T202737Z
UID:141779-1776189600-1776195000@www.gardinermuseum.on.ca
SUMMARY:The Gardiner Transformed: Curator Tour and Hands-On Clay Session
DESCRIPTION:The Gardiner Transformed: Curator Tour and Hands-On Clay Session            \n                                    \n                                \n                        \n                                                \n                                                        Get Tickets                        \n                                            \n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n	\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Tuesday April 14\, 2026\n6:00 pm – 7:30 pm\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    In this exclusive after-hours experience\, Chief Curator & Deputy Director Dr. Sequoia Miller will lead a tour of the Museum’s transformed ground floor and Collection Galleries\, followed by an exploratory hands-on clay session. Be among the first to experience our new Makerspace! \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $34\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $40\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    About the Ground Floor Transformation \nIn November 2025\, the Gardiner Museum revealed our fully transformed ground floor\, marking the Museum’s most ambitious capital project in two decades. This once-in-a-generation renovation reimagined the Gardiner’ss role as an inspiring and accessible community-driven hub where clay serves as a bridge between cultures\, histories\, and people. Designed by Montgomery Sisam Architects and Andrew Jones Design\, in collaboration with architect Chris Cornelius of studio:indigenous\, the transformation of the Gardiner’s 9\,000-square-foot ground floor was guided by the principles of connectivity\, access\, and Indigeneity. It features new Collection Galleries\, a fully equipped Makerspace\, a Community Learning Centre\, and the Gardiner’s first-ever gallery of Indigenous ceramics.\nLearn more \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/the-gardiner-transformed-curator-tour-and-hands-on-clay-session-april-14-2026/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Programs & Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/wp-content/uploads/Ground-Floor-Tour-and-Clay-Workshop.jpg
GEO:43.6679938;-79.3935128
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Gardiner Museum 111 Queen's Park Toronto ON M5S 2C7 Canada;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=111 Queen's Park:geo:-79.3935128,43.6679938
END:VEVENT
