X-SOURCE:Meetup: Toronto Photography Group
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-photography-group/
UID:event_313762335@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260407T031644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260418T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260418T153000
SUMMARY:Special Event -Stairs and Arches- location workshop with Drew G
DESCRIPTION:The Toronto Photography Group\nAbout the event\n\n1:30pm 3:30p
 m session\nTickets available for this workshop at - [https://www.wtpg.ngo/
 event-details/special-event-stairs-and-arches-location-workshop-with-drew-
 g-session-2](https://www.wtpg.ngo/event-details/special-event-stairs-and-a
 rches-location-workshop-with-drew-g-session-2)\nStudio by House 1585 Brita
 nnia Road East L4W2M4\nLighting tech tbd\nModel Drew Gilder -[https://www.
 instagram.com/theonlydrewcatherine/?hl=en](https://www.instagram.com/theon
 lydrewcatherine/?hl=en)\nJoin us for this fun and educational location lig
 hting workshop with Drew G\, This will be a fun evening at Studio by House
  in Mississauga\n\n**Workshop Details:** This is an amazing opportunity to
  light and shoot an talented glamour model in a wonderfully styled studio 
 with some beautiful 3\,4 and 5 light set ups with Elinchrom modifiers . We
  will be creating 3x lighting set ups and creating some great art nude ima
 ges using modifiers to soften and shape the light .\nDo you aspire to lear
 n the secrets of beautiful and creative soft and crisp lighting techniques
  on location?\nWe are dedicated to lighting and sharing our photographic k
 nowledge with you. Our fun and informative group workshop with professiona
 l instructors is designed to cater to your interests. Throughout the works
 hop\, we will discuss the specific lighting setups for each scenario\, exp
 laining the choice of modifiers and angles to effectively illuminate the s
 ubject and accessories.\n\nStudio by House -\n\n\\*\\*Instructor:\\*\\*Phi
 l Sutherland **Assistant:** tbd **Model:** The exceptionally awesome Drew 
 Gilder. Her remarkable posing skills will contribute to creating stunning 
 images during the workshop.\nTo ensure a high-quality experience for parti
 cipants\, we are limiting the 2 hour workshop to a maximum of 8 participan
 ts.\n\nAs an indigenous-led\, not-for-profit arts group\, we are dedicated
  to serving the artistic community and advocating for the photographic art
 s. At our core\, we believe in sharing knowledge and the joy of photograph
 y with the community. We strive to make art accessible to everyone and wor
 k hard to bring arts programming to the community.\n\n**Workshop Details:*
 *\n\n* Maximum Participants: 8\n* Workshop Fee: CAD$97 plus hst and vendor
  fee\n\n**Items to Bring:**\n\n* Camera/Lenses of choice (DSLR\, medium fo
 rmat\, or mirrorless)\n* Fully charged battery\n* Freshly formatted memory
  card(s)\n* General lenses\n* Pen and paper (if you wish to take notes)\n\
 nSo that you know\, tripods or camera supports are not required for this w
 orkshop.\n**Triggers:** We provide wireless triggers for most mainstream c
 amera types. Please feel free to email us to confirm compatibility with yo
 ur camera.\n**Model Release:** A West Toronto Photography Group model rele
 ase form\, will be provided to each participant for non-commercial use and
  training purposes. The model will sign these forms\, and printed copies w
 ill be provided to each photographer.\n**Cancellation Policy:** Refunds wi
 ll be issued within 72 hours if we\, as organizers\, have to postpone or c
 ancel the event. We understand that sometimes circumstances prevent attend
 ance at a workshop. If you cannot attend\, please get in touch with us as 
 soon as possible\, and we will help you resell your workshop spot to the g
 roup. We will reimburse you for the ticket price if we can resell the tick
 et. However\, if we cannot resell the spot\, you may transfer it to someon
 e else to attend in your place\, but unfortunately\, no refund will be pro
 vided.\nWe look forward to welcoming you to this inspiring workshop and he
 lping you enhance your photography skills .
