SUMMARY: New Music for Old Hands Concert Series: Laura Gillis
DESCRIPTION:Matinee concert series at Labdara Lithuanian Nursing Home. Ea
 ch concert in this series will premiere a composition performed by the La
 bdara bell choir and Laura Gillis (conductor/pianist). Each composer will
  give a talk and share music with the residents and audience members\, fo
 llowed by a casual social mixer.\n\n2:00pm start time. Free Admission. Re
 serve your spot at Eventbrite. Limited seating available.\n\nApril 18: La
 ura Gillis\n\nLaura will be joined by friends on electric guitar and viol
 a da gamba to perform songs from her project\, Vividness. She will talk a
 bout the special projects\, Vintage Voices and New Music for Old Hands\, 
 that she has created to connect long-term care and art creation. The Labd
 ara bell choir and Laura will premiere three pieces that she has written 
 for bell choir and piano\, Untitled\, River and Depths\, and Time Passes\
 , Everything Changes.\n\nMay 2: Adam Scime\n\nMay 16: Louise Campbell (jo
 ining us virtually from Montreal)\n\nMay 30: Lieke van der Voort (joining
  us virtually from Germany)\n\nJune 13: Alex Eddington\n\nJune 20: Martin
  van de Ven\n\nwww.facebook.com/NewMusicForOldHands http://www.facebook.c
 om/NewMusicForOldHands
CATEGORIES:Music,Concert,#poweredbyTAC,#BringingTheArtsToLife
