SUMMARY:Creating Interactive Fiction with Twine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260427T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260427T200000
UID:69b310858d5e2d093364df48@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Choose your own adventure! In this hands-on workshop\, we'll b
 rowse examples of interactive fiction based on video games and touch on th
 e basics of storytelling. Then\, we'll create our own game using Twine\, a
 n open-source hypertext storytelling tool. Located in the 2nd floor eLearn
 ing Lab.\nRegistration is required for this class and begins April 13th\, 
 2026 at 12:30 pm.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes 
 of the start of the program.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal
  information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under
  the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inform
 ation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and 
 evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can b
 e directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 78
 9 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b310858d5e2d093364df48
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
