SUMMARY:Photo Editing with Adobe Photoshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T160000
UID:69b61b858d5e2d0933656101@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adobe Photoshop is the world’s best imaging and graphic desi
 gn software and is at the core of just about every creative project\, from
  photo editing and compositing to digital painting\, animation\, and graph
 ic design.\nJoin us for an introductory lesson and learn about the most co
 mmon tools. We'll explore the workspace and enhance images while investiga
 ting tools such as crop\, levels\, colour balance and more. See how an ima
 ge can be altered and repaired using patch tools such as the clone and hea
 ling brush tools. We'll also dive deep into the world of layers and how yo
 u can manage them for those really unique and fun projects.\nRegistration 
 will start 2 weeks before this class. Computers will be provided.\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Danforth/Coxwell\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b61b858d5e2d0933656101
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
