SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260407T031649Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T180000
SUMMARY:Toronto Mid-Town Weekend Gaming @ The Guild House
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Heavy Boardgamers\nWelcome to the Saturday meetup for 
 Toronto Heavy Boardgamers @ The Guild House!\n\nThe purpose of this event 
 is to meet up to play heavier / longer board games\, and have fun while do
 ing it! We will start off small and if there is sufficient interest we wil
 l add capacity for future events.\n\nYou are welcome to bring your own gam
 es to the event\, or use the games in the library at the location.\n\n**Sc
 heduling details:**\n\\- If you have a specific game that you would like t
 o post for\\\, feel free to do so in comments\\. In your post\\\, include 
 the name of the game\\\, number of players needed for the game\\\, whether
  you are offering a teach or not\\\, and the start time \\(please try to s
 tart before noon if possible\\)\\.\n\\- If you would like to join a specif
 ic game that has already been posted\\\, feel free to comment on it confir
 ming your participation\\. Make sure you have noted the details posted by 
 the host\\.\n\\- You are of course also welcome to organize / join games o
 nsite on the day itself\\\, assuming sufficient players / tables are avail
 able\n\n**Rules around COVID:**\n\\- Given this is a public event\\\, we r
 espectfully ask that only i\\) fully vaccinated individuals\\\, and ii\\) 
 those not exhibiting any COVID symptoms\\\, participate\\. This requiremen
 t may change in the future based on provincial guidelines and group requir
 ements\n\n**Available Amenities:**\n\\- Food and drinks are available on\\
 -site\\\, you can see a detailed menu [here](https://theguildhouse.ca/page
 s/menu). **Outside food and drinks are not allowed by the Guild House.**\n
 \\- There is an on\\-site game library\\\, and use of it is covered within
  the admission fee\\.\n\n**Admission Fee:**\n\\- There is a $10 fee charge
 d by the establishment for use of space\\. Payments are to be made directl
 y to the establishment at the time of entry and not to the organizer
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-heavy-boardgamers/events/tqhs
 ttyjchbdb/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20251103T001733Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251103T001733Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b43e7e8089f23c6761d866"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Appleseed Yoga: Yoga Storytime
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T120000
UID:69b43e7e8089f23c6761d866@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an interactive\, movement-based program where we r
 ead stories and make them come alive with our bodies! Join Megan Snider\, 
 author and Founder of Appleseed Yoga for Kids as she delivers inspiring st
 ories and gets the whole family moving. Class begins and ends with song an
 d breathwork and is filled with pages of creativity and activity. Kids and
  families can sit quietly and listen\, do partial poses or make up their o
 wn\, following our lead. It's ALL yoga! No experience\, mats\, or material
 s required.\nDrop-in.\nUnfortunately\, we cannot accommodate any large gro
 ups/daycares for this program.\nIf you identify as a person with a disabil
 ity and require an accessibility accommodation to participate in this prog
 ram\, please contact Accessibility Services by email\, accessibleservices@
 tpl.ca\, or voicemail\, 416-393-7099\, to make a request. Please contact u
 s at least three weeks in advance.
LOCATION:Jones\, Children's Area
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b43e7e8089f23c6761d866
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cdb47a1e64afd01e66485d"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Introduction to 3D Printing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T123000
UID:69cdb47a1e64afd01e66485d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how 3D printers work and how you can print at the Toront
 o Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hubs. This class includes hands-on
  instruction with Prusa Slicer\, the software used to prepare your 3D obje
 ct file for printing on a Prusa MK3S+ 3D printer.\nDROP IN\nNote: Customer
 s are no longer required to attend a mandatory 3D printing class prior to 
 using a 3D printer at the Toronto Public Library’s Digital Innovation Hu
 bs. This class is for those who are interested in learning more about 3D p
 rinting and how to use the Prusa software.
LOCATION:Long Branch\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cdb47a1e64afd01e66485d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1659f2866a5b48843df0b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:FRESH Movie Saturdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T130000
UID:69c1659f2866a5b48843df0b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Come join us every Saturday for screenings of your favourite movies. In ad
 dition to this\, enjoy cuddles with a therapy dog! Therapy dog Goose visi
 ts Fort York Branch on alternate Saturdays from 11:00AM-12:00PM.\nWe'll b
 e showing the following films:\nApril 4-Honey I Shrunk the Kids\nApril 11-
 Hachi:A Dog's Tale\nApril 18-Zootopia\nApril 25-How to Train Your Dragon(2
 010)\nMay 2-Wonder\nMay 9-Stuart Little\nMay 16-The Jungle Book(1967)\nMay
  23-The Water Horse\nMay 30-Two Brothers\nDrop-ins are welcome.\nThis prog
 ram is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiati
 ve\n.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Urban Living Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1659f2866a5b48843df0b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1a19ab6c4ac1fedc7addb"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Girls Coding
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T130000
UID:69c1a19ab6c4ac1fedc7addb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program introduces children to beginner computer programm
 ing and fosters the development of essential STEM skills. Delivered in col
 laboration with Macaulay Centres for Children\, the initiative focuses on 
 promoting educational growth and enhancing future employment opportunities
 \, particularly for children in marginalized communities. Participants wil
 l engage in hands-on coding activities\, make new friends\, and have fun i
 n a supportive. Space is limited\, and advance registration with a commitm
 ent to attend the full session is required.
LOCATION:Woodview Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1a19ab6c4ac1fedc7addb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
