SUMMARY:Together Toronto (Pre-Event: Exclusive Session for Y Combinator S2
 6 Applicants)
DESCRIPTION:TechTO\n**This is a paid event. You must register and have a t
 icket to attend.** 👉 [https://luma.com/together-toronto-may-4-2026](htt
 ps://luma.com/together-toronto-may-4-2026)\n\n**Together Toronto - the sto
 ries behind how companies actually get built here.**\n\nTogether Toronto b
 rings founders onto the stage to share what building in this city really l
 ooks like. Honest conversations about pivots\, hard calls\, and lessons le
 arned\, from people who've figured out how to keep moving.\n\n***\n\n**Age
 nda**\n5:00–6:00 pm — YC S26 Applicant Session (selected founders only
 )\n6:00–7:00 pm — Doors open\, networking\n7:00–8:30 pm — Communit
 y open mic\, speaker presentations & fireside chat\n8:30–9:00 pm — Net
 working\n9:00 pm — Afterparty (offsite)\n\n***\n\n***Speakers***\n\n**JJ
  Tang** (Rootly) — founder of an AI-native incident management platform 
 trusted by LinkedIn\, NVIDIA\, Canva\, DoorDash and others. Forbes 30 Unde
 r 30. YC alum. 400% YoY revenue growth and a $15M Series A.\n\n**Mark Hlad
 y** (SimpleHedge) — serial founder. His last company\, Tripleplay\, was 
 acquired by Roblox in 2022. Previously Product Lead at Facebook and Engage
 ment Manager at McKinsey.\n\n*More speakers to be announced.*\n\n***\n\n**
 *YC S26 Applicants - there's a session for you***\n\nLed by YC alumni\, th
 is one-hour pre-event gives active S26 applicants focused feedback on thei
 r application before the deadline. Spots are limited and require approval.
 \n\n**Select the YC (S26) Applicant Pass when registering.**\n\n*TechTO is
  not affiliated with\, sponsored by\, or endorsed by Y Combinator.*\n\n***
 \n\n**This is a paid event. You must register and have a ticket to attend.
 ** 👉 [https://luma.com/together-toronto-may-4-2026](https://luma.com/to
 gether-toronto-may-4-2026)\n\n*By attending you consent to photography and
  video recording and agree to receive the TechTO newsletter. Tickets are n
 on-transferable and non-refundable.*
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/techto/events/313639014/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260304T214031Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260304T214031Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a72bdc8089f23c675f88e7"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:AI and the Environment with Han Qiao
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260504T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260504T210000
UID:69a72bdc8089f23c675f88e7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join our Innovator in Residence\, Joel S. Silver\, in conversa
 tion with Han Qiao about AI and the environment.\nHan Qiao is a PhD candid
 ate at the University of Toronto\, Faculty of Information\, and a member o
 f the Just Sustainability Design Lab. Han’s current research sits in the
  intersection of human-computer interaction\, design and urban planning. H
 er ongoing projects look into how people interact with data and data tools
  to imagine and navigate sustainable futures. Previously\, Han has conduct
 ed research in designing creativity support tools and investigating questi
 ons related to human-AI interaction.\nThis program is part of the Innovato
 r in Residence (AI and Music Production) program\, which is designed to he
 lp beginner and intermediate learners build knowledge and creative skills 
 and get hands-on with current AI tools in music production and learn about
  the history\, copyright and ethics of generative music. For more informat
 ion and a full list of programs\, visit\ntpl.ca/airesident\n.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a72bdc8089f23c675f88e7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
