BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/695c3a6cc719ac98c336176b"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696abaf8b0595799c096d203"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:After School Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T163000
UID:696abaf8b0595799c096d203@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our Afte
 r School Club and learn new things\, make stuff\, meet other kids and have
  fun! For ages\n6-12.\nDrop-in.\nUpcoming Programs:\nMarch 31 - Easter Bun
 ny Masks\nApril 7 - Bulldozing with Dash\nSnacks are offered during the A
 fter School Club for participants.\nFood may contain or have come into con
 tact with common allergens. Ingredient lists will be available. Snacks are
  generously supported\, in part\, by donors.\nIf you or your child lives w
 ith a disability\, and requires an accessibility accommodation to particip
 ate in this program\, please contact Accessibility Services by email\, acc
 essibleservices@tpl.ca\, or voicemail\, 416-393-7099\, to make a request. 
 Please contact us at least three weeks in advance.
LOCATION:Jones
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696abaf8b0595799c096d203
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6967cef8c719ac98c336e382"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Video Games
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T154500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T190000
UID:6967cef8c719ac98c336e382@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in to the Youth Hub every Tuesday and Thursday to play vi
 deo games. Play with friends\, by yourself\, or maybe someone new.\nTuesda
 ys will be Nintendo Switch days and Thursdays will be PS4 days.\n*NEW* Sta
 rting at 3:30 pm\, teens can sign up for a time slot to use the consoles. 
 If there is no demand\, gaming will be awarded on a first come first serve
  basis.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welco
 ming place for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff 
 are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop b
 y a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6967cef8c719ac98c336e382
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ce83c82866a5b48845f760"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:After School Role-Playing Games: Mausritter
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T170000
UID:69ce83c82866a5b48845f760@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You are tiny mice seeking adventure and renown in a huge and p
 erilous world of swords and sorcery. Will you and your companions prevail 
 over dangerous enemies many times your size? Or will it fall to others to 
 finish the job? In the likely event one of your mice should come to a grim
  demise\, you can quickly create a new one and keep on playing.\n*Registra
 tion is required. Ages 8-12 strongly recommended.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Room B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ce83c82866a5b48845f760
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cb03248089f23c6765a97c"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Fun with Snap Circuits
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T170000
UID:69cb03248089f23c6765a97c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Play with electricity and circuitry during this hands-on progr
 am! Turn on a light\, spin a motor\, activate a speaker and choose from hu
 ndreds of different projects\, or try making your own circuits! For childr
 en ages 6-12.
LOCATION:Humber Summit
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cb03248089f23c6765a97c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69711d50992fc18a86deb18d"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Board Game Café
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T180000
UID:69711d50992fc18a86deb18d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Youth Hub every Tuesday to play board games wit
 h your friends! Ask us for our list of board games\, and check our monthly
  calendar for Tournaments with prizes! All materials provided.\nThis progr
 am is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teen
 s after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always availabl
 e. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\n
 Youth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Eatonville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69711d50992fc18a86deb18d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cdb52a4dacf581ff85f2b1"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Lego Spike for kids 9-12
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T170000
UID:69cdb52a4dacf581ff85f2b1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Dive into hands-on STEM fun by building and coding interactive
  LEGO SPIKE models. Working in teams\, children 8-12 will solve exciting c
 hallenges and bring their creations to life!\nInformation Collection Notic
 e:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your i
 nformation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 4
 16-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Long Branch\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cdb52a4dacf581ff85f2b1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cd24ebfca21471b7ede44b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Digital LEGO Creation for Kids
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T170000
UID:69cd24ebfca21471b7ede44b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Using the Bricklinks Studio app\, kids will learn how they can
  design and create their own digital LEGO creations in a 3D design workspa
 ce.\nThis program was design for children ages 8 and up.\nRegistration is 
 required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on thi
 s form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librari
 es Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be 
 used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questio
 ns about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answe
 rline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, To
 ronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Leaside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cd24ebfca21471b7ede44b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69af3d918089f23c6760f85b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Botanical Painting on Book Pages
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T180000
UID:69af3d918089f23c6760f85b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Turn pages of old discarded books into works of art in this mi
 x media workshop. Learn to create drawings and paintings of botanical obje
 cts such as flowers and berries in pen and watercolour. Whether you're a b
 eginner or an experienced artist\, you'll learn techniques for sketching b
 otanical subjects with fine pen details\, and then adding vibrant\, fluid 
 watercolours to bring them to life.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub ser
 vice. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the s
 ummer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snack
 s are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the bran
 ch to find out more.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, Youth Hub\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69af3d918089f23c6760f85b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bc760fbfe6da104224a32c"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:After School Fun
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T170000
UID:69bc760fbfe6da104224a32c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Spend your afternoon exploring STEM activities\, creating fun 
 crafts\, building with LEGO\, and making new friends — with something di
 fferent every week! For kids 6–12.\nDrop-in\, no registration required.\
 nMarch 24: Children's Graphic Novel Book Club\nApril 7: LEGO\nApril 14: 
 LEGO\nApril 21: Robotics\nApril 28: Children's Graphic Novel Book Club
LOCATION:High Park\, Community Room
