BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a8c194b48451fc3c06bf4f"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Music and AI for Kids!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T170000
UID:69a8c194b48451fc3c06bf4f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For ages 8-12.\nJoin us for 4 weeks of goofy\, musical fun! Ou
 r Innovator in Residence\, Joel S. Silver\, will show you how AI works to 
 help you create music. Create songs with the silliest lyrics you can think
  of\, create a soundtrack for your own skits\, even write a theme song fo
 r the library! No music or computer experience needed - just bring your cr
 eativity!\nDrop-in. No registration required\, but space is limited.\nThis
  program is part of the Innovator in Residence (AI and Music Production) p
 rogram\, which is designed to help beginner and intermediate learners buil
 d knowledge and creative skills and get hands-on with current AI tools in 
 music production and learn about the history\, copyright and ethics of gen
 erative music. For more information and a full list of programs\, visit\nt
 pl.ca/airesident\n.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a8c194b48451fc3c06bf4f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bafdb5ad384e40edb5408b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Discovery Club: Coding with Dash
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T170000
UID:69bafdb5ad384e40edb5408b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a super fun coding adventure with Dash! In this wo
 rkshop series\, we will learn the basics of programming using block coding
  and the Dash robot. Each week we will explore new challenges as we code D
 ash to move\, light up\, make sounds\, and complete obstacle courses.\nThi
 s program is for ages 9 to 12 years old.\nInformation Collection Notice:\n
 The personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public L
 ibrary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d)
 . The information will only be used for event and program registration\, d
 elivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your infor
 mation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-3
 97-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Lower level program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bafdb5ad384e40edb5408b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bd82ffb6c4ac1fedc70e25"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Choose Your Own Craft
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T180000
UID:69bd82ffb6c4ac1fedc70e25@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us every Tuesday to express your creativity! Bring your 
 friends and choose from our broad range of craft materials to make your o
 wn unique creation.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs
  are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\, where he
 lpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered dai
 ly. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out mor
 e.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bd82ffb6c4ac1fedc70e25
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c7e1ad9057005337d0eafa"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Digital Painting II: Forms in Still Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T193000
UID:69c7e1ad9057005337d0eafa@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this advanced workshop participants will be taken step by s
 tep through creating a still life digital painting from a photo reference
  in Adobe Photoshop. We will be using a Wacom drawing tablet. The instruct
 or will touch base on important art principles relating to form\, that wil
 l be applied to painting in Adobe Photoshop.\nPrior experience with drawin
 g tablets and Photoshop is required for this class. Though\, we will brief
 ly go over the user interface and various tools we will be using. If you a
 re looking for an introduction class or an in depth look at the broader a
 spects of Photoshop please look out for our\nDigital Painting I: Introduct
 ion & Pen Control\nor\nIntroduction to Photo Editing in Photoshop\nprogram
 s.\nFor more information about this program please contact dihonline@tpl.c
 a.
LOCATION:Black Creek\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c7e1ad9057005337d0eafa
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
