SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Boba Drink Making
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T170000
UID:69b476da491b809c6f203dd1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to prepare a classic milk bubble tea\, including dec
 orating and mixing techniques\, as well as the breakdown of core ingredien
 ts. A classic lidded cup and straw will be provided to enjoy the boba as y
 ou go!\n*Please note this program contains dairy*\nThis program is part of
  Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after schoo
 l and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nu
 tritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor
  call the branch to find out more.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
 information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliver
 y and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information
  can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-598
 1\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69b476da491b809c6f203dd1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
