BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a1d9706724c63d00f59721"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Mad Science Workshop - Bugs!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T150000
UID:69a1d9706724c63d00f59721@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore the world of arthropods! Children examine insect anato
 my up close and classify creepy crawlers into insects and non-insects. At 
 habitat stations\, they build insect puzzles\, discover how insects see\, 
 spread pollen\, and defend themselves\, and uncover the science behind the
 se fascinating creatures. Also\, you can take home a model insect!\nFor sc
 hool-age children (5-12) and their caregivers. Drop-in.\nUnfortunately\, w
 e cannot accommodate any large groups/daycares at this time.\nIf you or yo
 ur child lives with a disability\, and requires an accessibility accommoda
 tion to participate in this program\, please contact Accessibility Service
 s by email\naccessibleservices@tpl.ca\n\, or voicemail\, 416-393-7099\, to
  make a request. Please contact us at least three weeks in advance.
LOCATION:Jones\, Children's Area
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a1d9706724c63d00f59721
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c4217d2866a5b488445c98"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:P.A. Day Soccer Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T150000
UID:69c4217d2866a5b488445c98@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the beautiful game and global culture with a soccer 
 party! Test your knowledge of world flags and tournament history with an i
 nteractive trivia game. Fill out your own tournament bracket with your win
 ner predictions\, then take a picture in our photo booth. You can even try
  your hand at playing soccer with robots! Feel free to represent the count
 ry you are supporting with shirts\, flags\, scarves\, homemade signs\, or 
 however else you like.\nFor children ages 6-12.\nInformation Collection No
 tice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto P
 ublic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, an
 d 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrat
 ion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles you
 r information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\
 , 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c4217d2866a5b488445c98
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
