X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Video Game Café
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T180000
UID:6971201c91e4576f847de1dc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Youth Hub every Friday to play video games on o
 ur Nintendo Switch or PS5 with your friends! Ask us for our list of video 
 games\, and check our monthly calendar for Gaming Tournaments with prizes!
 \nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming pl
 ace for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are alw
 ays available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a bra
 nch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Eatonville
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6971201c91e4576f847de1dc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69612a7f6f926136000f424e"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69603a014a9fd98b7f767547"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:After School Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T170000
UID:69603a014a9fd98b7f767547@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something to do after school? Come out to our Afte
 r School Club and learn new things\, make stuff\, meet other kids and have
  fun! For ages\n6-12.\nSnacks are offered during the After School Club for
  participants. Ingredient lists will be available. Snacks are generously s
 upported\, in part\, by donors.
LOCATION:St. Clair/Silverthorn\, This program takes place in the upstairs 
 program room.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69603a014a9fd98b7f767547
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696d1b2b76261f28006526b7"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_events
SUMMARY:Seniors E-Connect
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260605T180000
UID:696d1b2b76261f28006526b7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you 55+? Do you have a phone\, tablet or computer you don'
 t know how to use or want to learn to use better? Do you enjoy meeting new
  people?\nSeniors E-Connect will help you learn tech topics in a fun group
  setting\, but with the one-on-one help of a teen volunteer.
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, FCCR (First-Floor Auditorium)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/696d1b2b76261f28006526b7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library
END:VEVENT
