BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Thescifibookclub": "https://www.meetup.com/thescifibookclub/events/312950259/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_thescifibookclub
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Sci Fi Book Club
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.meetup.com/thescifibookclub/
UID:event_312950259@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260407T031651Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260628T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260628T160000
SUMMARY:Station Eleven - Emily St. John Mandel
DESCRIPTION:The Sci Fi Book Club\nHi everyone\,\n\nOur novel for June came
  in at a close second for contemporary picks on our survey. The story take
 s place around a devastating flu pandemic that threatens society as we kno
 w it. It's often cited as one of the more prophetic novels of recent times
 \, but takes things well beyond the covid pandemic.\n\nBook of the Month\n
 *Station Eleven -* Emily St. John Mandel (2014)\n\nFrom [Grimdark Magazine
 ](https://www.grimdarkmagazine.com/review-station-eleven-by-emily-st-john-
 mandel/)\, "*Station Eleven* by Emily St. John Mandel takes the best parts
  of the dystopian science fiction and fantasy genre and does one thing mos
 t books can’t\, give the reader hope." I really like the way [A Little B
 ook Problem](https://alittlebookproblem.co.uk/2023/08/04/book-review-stati
 on-eleven-by-emily-st-john-mandel-book-6-of-20booksofsummer/#:~:text=The%2
 0book%20is%20a%20beautiful%2C\,to%20in%20a%20world%20when)'s review descri
 bes the tone. "The book is a beautiful\, heart-wrenching and moving explor
 ation of what is important to us in life\, what we would hang on to in a w
 orld when almost everything we know and care about is torn away\, and what
  kind of people we discover we are in the face of great adversity."\n\n*St
 ation Eleven* shows how science fiction isn’t just about the future. It
 ’s about how we live today\, and the threads that connect us all. It's a
  celebration of the arts and bound to be a great conversation. I look forw
 ard to discussing this one with you!\n\nTo join a Book Club meeting\, all 
 you will need is YOURSELF. If you haven’t had a chance to finish the boo
 k\, we still would love for you to join us in the discussion.\n\nNot able 
 to join us in person for events? [The Sci Fi Book Club is on Discord](http
 s://discord.gg/B9NMnC2F). Join us and keep the conversation going.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/thescifibookclub/events/312950259/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260119T011018Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260119T011018Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
